{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Draw near to the altar.</b> For the Satan was showing him the image of a calf, and he was afraid lest he be unfit for the service. Moses said to him: Draw near to the altar and do not fear, for HaShem has chosen you." "<b>And make atonement for yourself and for the people.</b> This requires investigation, for this offering came only on behalf of Aaron, and the offering of the people is stated immediately after, as it is written: ״ועשה את קרבן העם וכפר בעדם״ — if so, why was it necessary to write 'and for the people'? And one may answer that it comes to give the reason why he should offer his own offering first, before the congregation — so that a meritorious one may come and make atonement for the sin. And this is what Moses said to him: ״and make atonement for yourself,״ and then, once you are meritorious, you will be able to make atonement through the offering of the people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:55.272586362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}